<div class="ed-reading guide-reading text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Start with the account you can access now and make a few safe comparisons. An email app is only the viewing and sending tool. The email provider stores the mailbox. For example, Outlook can be the app used to access a Gmail account. That distinction helps you test the right place without making a destructive change.</p>
<section class="ed-start" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading"><p class="ed-label">Start here</p><h2 id="start-heading">Start with the least disruptive checks</h2><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use these checks in order. Stop when you find a clear difference, and keep sign-in recovery as a separate problem.</p><div class="ed-choices">
{{ choice("Compare mailbox and app", "Open the provider's webmail in the current browser, then compare it with the app on the same account.", "#check-connection", "startup", "/img/guides/email-troubleshooting-v1.webp", "A laptop displaying a conceptual email inbox.", "Read this part") }}
