</div></section>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="check-connection"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Check the connection and the mailbox</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">First confirm that the device can open a few ordinary websites. If everything is slow or offline, email may only be showing the wider connection problem. If other websites work, open your provider's webmail in the browser. Use the provider's normal sign-in page and the account you intend to check.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If new messages appear in webmail but not in the app, the mailbox may be working while the app is not updating. If neither webmail nor the app shows new mail, the issue may be with the provider, account access, storage or the sender's delivery attempt. A message that has not reached the provider cannot be recovered from the app.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For a wider connection fault, see <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-dropouts-diagnosis/">Wi-Fi dropouts diagnosis</a>.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="compare-app-provider"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Understand the app and provider</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The app on your phone or computer is not necessarily the company that provides your email. Outlook may be the app while Gmail is the provider. Apple Mail may display an account hosted elsewhere. This is why webmail is a useful comparison: it checks the mailbox without relying on the app's local display or sync state.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On Android Gmail, pulling down can request a refresh. Google also recommends checking that the app is current, restarting the device, and checking Menu → Settings → your account → Data usage → Sync Gmail. Sync is not always instant. The device's available storage is also different from the shared storage quota for the Google account. See the <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/6383854?hl=en">Gmail troubleshooting guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On current iPhone and iPad software, Settings → Apps → Mail → Mail Accounts → Fetch New Data controls when mail is checked. Settings → Notifications → Mail controls alerts. They do not prove that a message reached the provider. Apple also warns that a backup preserves mail settings rather than the email itself. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/102578">Apple's Mail troubleshooting guidance</a>.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="check-safe-limits"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Check storage, status and access separately</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Look for a clear storage warning in webmail or the provider's account page. A full provider mailbox can prevent sending or receiving. For Outlook.com, messages sent while the mailbox is full may bounce and do not automatically reappear after space is later available. This applies to the Outlook.com service, not to every account viewed in the Outlook app. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/can-t-send-or-receive-email-in-outlook-com">Microsoft's Outlook.com guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Also check the provider's status page if the mailbox itself is unavailable. Do not treat a sign-in problem as a sync problem. If you cannot access the account, use the provider's official recovery route rather than repeatedly changing app settings.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Keep the safe boundary") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not delete the account, remove or rebuild the mail profile, clear app storage, disable two-step verification, weaken spam protection, or change unfamiliar security settings while troubleshooting. If local mail, contacts or calendars may not be fully synced, pause and get help before changing the device.</p>{% endcall %}
